claim.claim-text:
CLAIMS 1. Apparatus for in-line heat treatment of elongated metal stock hot rolled in a rolling mill comprising in-line with the rolling mill: a) a first shear to cut the rolled stock into pieces of predetermined length, b) a quenching box for forced cooling of hot rolled stock, c) a layer preparation system to layer a predetermined number of pieces of cut stock in preparation for further heat treatment thereof, d) an on-line annealing furnace for controlled cooling, holding or heating of the layers of stock, e) means to discharge and separate the layers into individual pieces of stock, and f) a cooling bed for cooling the heat treated stock. 2. Apparatus according to claim 1 , wherein the quenching box is connected with the cooling bed. 3. Apparatus according to claim 1 , further comprising an induction heater disposed between the quenching box and the layer preparation system. 4. Apparatus according to claim 1 , further comprising an in-line low thermocontrolled rolling device including water boxes, equalization zone and reduction and sizing block means disposed between the rolling mill and the first shear. 5. Apparatus according to claim 4, further comprising into the thermocontrolled rolling device, between the equalization zone and the reduction and sizing block means, a second shear to cut the lead and the tail of the rolled stock coming from the rolling train. 6. Apparatus according to claim 1 , wherein the cooling bed is a controlled atmosphere cooling bed for cooling the heat treated stock in a protective atmosphere. 7. Apparatus according to claim 1 , wherein the stock is in the form of bar product. 8. A method for in-line heat treating of steel stock hot rolled in a rolling mill, comprising the steps, conducted in-line with the rolling mill, of: a. cutting the rolled stock into pieces of predetermined length; b. quenching the pieces of hot rolled stock in a quenching box; 

c. in preparation for tempering of the quenched stock, preparing layers of predetermined numbers of pieces of stock in a layers preparation zone wherein the number of cut pieces of stock per layer depends on the section of the rolled stock; d. tempering the prepared layers of stock in an on-line annealing furnace for controlled cooling, holding or heating of the layers of stock; e. separating and discharging the layers into individual pieces of quenched and tempered stock, and f. cooling the quenched and tempered stock in a cooling bed. 9. A method according to claim 8, wherein the pieces of hot rolled stock coming from the quenching box have a temperature in the range 50 to 150°C. 10. A method according to claim 8, wherein tempering takes place while holding the layers of stock at a temperature in the range 500 to 700°C for a time about 60 minutes to about 120 minutes. 11. A method according to claim 8, further comprising the step of induction heating the rolled and quenched stock before preparing layers to help the following tempering of the rolled stock in the heat treatment furnace. 12. A method according to claim 8 for producing quenched stock in the quenching zone, including by-passing steps c) to e) of claim 8, and passing the quenched stock directly to the cooling zone. 13. A method according to claim 12, wherein the forced cooling in the water box is started from a temperature of about 800°C. 14. A method for in-line treating of steel stock hot rolled in a rolling mill, comprising the steps conducted in-line with the rolling mill, of: a. in-line treating the rolled stock, before shearing, in the thermocontrolled rolling zone, thereby preparing a product having a spherodized preliminary section; b. cutting the low temperature rolled stock into pieces of predetermined length; c. in preparation for annealing of the termocontrolled rolled stock, preparing layers of predetermined numbers of pieces of stock in a layers preparation zone wherein the number of cut pieces of stock per layer depends on the section of the rolled stock; 

d. annealing the prepared layers of stock in an on-line annealing furnace for controlled cooling, holding or heating of the layers of stock; e. separating and discharging the layers into individual pieces of annealed stock, and f. cooling the annealed stock in a cooling bed. 15. A method according to claim 14 for producing spherodized annealed stock, wherein the thermocontrolled rolling step takes place in the thermocontrolled rolling zone in the range of from about 750 to about 850°C and the spherodizing occurs in the on-line annealing furnace at a temperature in the range of from about 680 to about 720°C and a holding time of about 60 minutes to about 120 minutes. 16. A method according to claim 14 for workability or shearability annealing the stock, wherein the thermocontrolled rolling step takes place in the thermocontrolled rolling zone in the range of about 750 to about 850°C and the annealing occurs in the on-line annealing furnace at a temperature in the range of about 630 to about 680°C and a holding time of about 30 minutes to about 40 minutes. 17. A method according to claim 14 for producing recrystallized annealed stock wherein the thermocontrolled rolling step takes place in the termocontrolled rolling zone in the range of from about 750 to about 850°C and the annealing occurs in the on-line annealing furnace at a temperature in the range of from about 700 to about 800°C and a holding time of about 30 minutes to about 60 minutes. 18. A method according to either one of claim 8 or claim 14, further comprising a subsequent in-line finishing step selected from the group consisting of final cooling in a water box, shotblasting, cutting to final form, and packaging. 19. A method according to either one of claim 8 or claim 14, wherein the cooling zone is provided with a protective atmosphere.
